# Accepted (NY4I 2026-10-17): an ADIF exchange tag the contest does not declare is not written; and (2026-10-23) an ARRL_SECT that is not an ADIF 3.1.6 section is not written; and (2026-11-15) a Canadian province is written in ADIF <STATE>, which D7 omitted
#
# TContestBase.EmitADIFReceivedFields writes PRECEDENCE and NAME only where the class's
# ReceivedExchangeFields declares them; Winter Field Day's does not (class and section).
# D7 wrote every non-empty field, and this log holds five QSOs with a stray value: four
# PRECEDENCE (Y, A, A, A) and one NAME (Dan). docs/CONTEST_OWNERSHIP_DESIGN.md 8.2w.
#
# ADIF 3.1.6 (2026-10-23): ARRL_SECT is an enumeration, and five QSOs here carry
# a value that is not in it -- MD (twice), NY, IO and DC, as typed. The export
# writes ARRL_SECT only for a real section, so those five lose the tag; the
# typed text stays in QTH and SRX_STRING. tools/adifvalidator rejected them.
#
# ref.adi is D7-written and NEVER regenerated, so these records are pinned here
# as the exact expected difference: the stray tags are gone and nothing else changes.
#
# Read by run-golden-diff.sh AND test-adif-roundtrip.sh through known-pin-lib.sh: the lines
# below the comments are EXACTLY the changed lines of ref.adi vs the candidate.
#
# Accepted (NY4I 2026-11-15, issue 275): a VE station's province is its ADIF <STATE>
# (ADIF 3.1.6 lists the Canadian provinces under DXCC 1 for STATE). D7 wrote QTH only, so
# the 32 VE records here gain <STATE:2>xx; nothing else on them changes.
